    "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Install Corepack before using the Node 26 base images**\n\nBoth Docker builds still depend on the bundled `corepack` executable: `Dockerfile:25` runs `corepack enable && corepack prepare --activate`, and `Dockerfile.dev:28` runs `corepack enable`, with neither installing Corepack first. [Node.js documents](https://nodejs.org/download/release/v25.8.0/docs/api/corepack.html) that \u201cCorepack will no longer be distributed starting with Node.js v25,\u201d and the [Node 26 slim image definition](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nodejs/docker-node/main/26/trixie-slim/Dockerfile) does not add it separately. Consequently, switching these base images to 26 breaks both builds with `corepack: not found` before dependency installation. Install Corepack explicitly, or provision the pinned pnpm version another way, in both Dockerfiles.\n\nUseful? React with \ud83d\udc4d\u00a0/ \ud83d\udc4e.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->",
