    "body": "Valid. I ran both images:\n\n```\n$ docker run --rm node:26-slim sh -c 'node --version; command -v corepack || echo \"corepack: not found\"; ls /usr/local/lib/node_modules'\nv26.13.0\ncorepack: not found\nnpm\n```\n\n`node:26` (used by `Dockerfile.dev`) gives the same output. So `corepack enable` at `Dockerfile:25` and `Dockerfile.dev:28` fail with exit 127. No PR check builds these images. The first build would be the `next` image (`publish.yml` \u2192 `publish-dev.yml` \u2192 `docker.yml`) on the merge push to unstable, plus the nightly Kurtosis run, so both would break right after merge.\n\nThe smallest fix that keeps the `packageManager` pin:\n\n```dockerfile\nRUN npm install -g corepack && corepack enable && corepack prepare --activate && \\\n```\n\nThe same applies to `Dockerfile.dev`. `docs/pages/faqs.md` also tells users to run `corepack enable`. On Node 26 that needs `npm install -g corepack` first, so it's worth updating with the installation docs in this PR.\n\nSeparately, the Benchmark job on this PR runs on Node 26.13.0 against a Node 24 baseline, so its one regression (`phase0 processEffectiveBalanceUpdates - 250000 worstcase 0.5`, x3.2) compares across runtimes. It may be runner noise, but a local A/B of that bench on both versions would settle it.\n",
